---
description: Prepare revision-bound resource, staff, and public event operations from a proved run sheet.
args:{event:EventProductionState;proof:RunSheetProof;checkpoint:LiveCheckpoint;sourceEventId:string;venueId:string;producerId:string}
returns:LiveEventEffectPreparation
---
Return `{effects:[], checkpoint}` if the event is in emergency suspension, `event.id` or `checkpoint.eventId` differs from sourceEventId, event or checkpoint identity otherwise differs, the run sheet revision is absent, or proof has any double-booked resource, broken dependency, setup conflict, or venue-close overrun. These conditions require a source-owned repair before an adapter sees an operation.

For each resource required by the event's accepted run sheet, compare its exact ID with checkpoint.reservedResourceIds. Prepare one `reserve-event-resources` intention for only the missing IDs, with `eventId: sourceEventId`, numeric `eventRevision: event.revision`, and string `runSheetRevision: checkpoint.runSheetRevision`. Set its idempotency key to `reserve-event-resources:<eventId>:<eventRevision>:<runSheetRevision>:<sorted-missing-resource-ids>`; never reuse this key for another effect kind or different resource set. Never infer a reservation receipt from an intention.

For each role required by the changed segments, inspect checkpoint.acknowledgements for that role and exact runSheetRevision. Request updates only from roles with no received acknowledgement for this revision. Preserve pending and conflicting acknowledgements as unresolved; do not turn either into consent. Bind the effect to eventId, numeric eventRevision and string runSheetRevision. Use a key `request-role-acknowledgements:<eventId>:<eventRevision>:<runSheetRevision>:<sorted-role-ids>` so it remains distinct from resource reservation and publication.

Prepare `publish-event-revision` only when checkpoint.producerApprovalRevision equals checkpoint.runSheetRevision, every required resource has an actual reservation ID recorded in checkpoint, and every required role has a received acknowledgement for that same revision. Otherwise prepare only the eligible reservation or acknowledgement intentions. Include eventId, numeric eventRevision and string runSheetRevision. Use key `publish-event-revision:<eventId>:<eventRevision>:<runSheetRevision>`, distinct from both other operations. Bind all intentions to the source eventId, venueId, producerId and exact revision; omit public content not present in the accepted event plan. Return `{effects, checkpoint}` with the unchanged checkpoint so prepared intentions cannot be mistaken for received acknowledgements or reservations.
